@tradition bridge-hour
// Bridge hour: every fourth Tuesday (week 4 of the cycle: days 23, 51, 79...), just after the day shift, Deck 1.
// Juniors visit the bridge for a while; the Captain comes up to say hello (Tuesday is one of her days off). Juniors only.
// The deck architect's places on the bridge (event: 'bridge-hour', standing along the rail) come first; until then,
// the bridge lobby and the observation room.
k: 461
title: Bridge hour
when: every 4 weeks tuesday week 4
at: 17:15-18:00
min: 20
where: 1 room Bridge lobby: event
where: 1 room Observation room: common-room, lounge-seat
who: marrow always, juniors 40%
anim: talk
host: marrow
from: marrow
invite: host=marrow odds=15% line="Bridge hour after shift. Come up and see where we steer from."

== mail
- Bridge hour tomorrow, {time}. Juniors are welcome on Deck 1 for a while: the helm, the charts and the view. I'll be there to say hello. Please don't touch anything red.

== ask
- Bridge hour later! I'm going to ask about the big chair.   #funny
- Juniors get to visit the bridge after shift. I've ironed my collar.   #funny
- The Captain says hello to everyone at bridge hour. Everyone.

== here
- That's the helm. Don't lean on it.   #funny
- You can see the whole bow from up here.
- The Captain knows everyone's name. How?

== thanks
- You stand on the bridge with the other juniors. The Captain shakes your hand and asks how you're finding the Wren.   #warm

== chatter
- At bridge hour the Captain asked about my bunk. My bunk!   #funny
- I touched the chart table at bridge hour. It was very ordinary. I loved it.   #warm
- One day I'll work up on the bridge. You watch.
